{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 21,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The king’s heart is in the hand of Jehovah as the watercourses:\nHe turneth it whithersoever he will.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every way of a man is right in his own eyes;\nBut Jehovah weigheth the hearts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To do righteousness and justice\nIs more acceptable to Jehovah than sacrifice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A high look, and a proud heart,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the lamp of the wicked, is sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The thoughts of the diligent ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "tend",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " only to plenteousness;\nBut every one that is hasty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hasteth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " only to want.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The getting of treasures by a lying tongue\nIs a vapor driven to and fro by them that seek death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The violence of the wicked shall sweep them away,\nBecause they refuse to do justice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The way of him that is laden with guilt is exceeding crooked;\nBut as for the pure, his work is right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop,\nThan with a contentious woman in a wide house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The soul of the wicked desireth evil:\nHis neighbor findeth no favor in his eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the scoffer is punished, the simple is made wise;\nAnd when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous man considereth the house of the wicked,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "How",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wicked are overthrown to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ruin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor,\nHe also shall cry, but shall not be heard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A gift in secret pacifieth anger;\nAnd a present in the bosom, strong wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is joy to the righteous to do justice;But it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding\nShall rest in the assembly of the dead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that loveth pleasure shall be a poor man:\nHe that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked is a ransom for the righteous;\nAnd the treacherous ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "cometh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the stead of the upright.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is better to dwell in a desert land,\nThan with a contentious and fretful woman.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is precious treasure and oil in the dwelling of the wise;\nBut a foolish man swalloweth it up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that followeth after righteousness and kindness\nFindeth life, righteousness, and honor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wise man scaleth the city of the mighty,\nAnd bringeth down the strength of the confidence thereof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue\nKeepeth his soul from troubles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The proud and haughty man, scoffer is his name;\nHe worketh in the arrogance of pride.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The desire of the sluggard killeth him;\nFor his hands refuse to labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is that coveteth greedily all the day long;\nBut the righteous giveth and withholdeth not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination;\nHow much more, when he bringeth it with a wicked mind!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A false witness shall perish;\nBut the man that heareth shall speak so as to endure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wicked man hardeneth his face;\nBut as for the upright, he establisheth his ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is no wisdom nor understanding\nNor counsel against Jehovah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.21.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.21.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The horse is prepared against the day of battle;\nBut victory is of Jehovah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
